  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rights and Resources Initiative (RRI) 2013-2017 - Rights and Resources Initative (RRI) 2013-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Rights and Resources Initiative (RRI) 2013-2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance of forest areas in developing countries for poverty reduction, biodiversity conservation and climate resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rights &amp; Resources Initiative (RRI) is a global coalition of org.s  working to encourage forest land tenure, policy and economic reforms  so that business reflects local development agendas and supports local livelihoods. RRI works at the country, regional and global      levels, collaborating on research, advocacy and convening strategic actors. Agreement partner is Rights &amp; Resources Group (RRG).

Clear and secure land tenure for local communities is an important precondition for several aspects of development, including sustainable use of natural resources, including decreased or avoided deforestation, increased resilience, economic development and enhancement of human rights and democratic societies. Special attention to securing women&#x2019;s rights is part of the intervention&apos;s design.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">&quot;Rights &amp; Resources Initiative&quot; (RRI) &#xe4;r en global sammanslutning av  f n 14 organisationer som vill fr&#xe4;mja skogliga &#xe4;gande- och nyttjander&#xe4;ttigheter, politiska och ekonomiska reformer s&#xe5; att sektorn &#xe5;terspeglar lokala utvecklingsagendor och st&#xf6;djer           lokalbefolkningens f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning gm forskning, opinionsbildning och strategiska samarbeten. Avtalspart &#xe4;r Rights &amp; Resources Group (RRG).

Klargjorda och s&#xe4;kra markr&#xe4;ttigheter f&#xf6;r lokal befolkning &#xe4;r en viktig f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttning f&#xf6;r en rad utvecklingsomr&#xe5;den, inkluderande h&#xe5;llbart nyttjande av naturresurser och minskad avskogning, &#xf6;kad resiliens, ekonomisk utveckling och fr&#xe4;mjandet av m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och demokratiska samh&#xe4;llen. S&#xe4;rskilt st&#xf6;d till att s&#xe4;kra kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter &#xe4;r en del av insatsens utformning.</narrative>
  </description>
